  "extraction_notes": "Cal Am corporate CCR format. Page 2 states 'in 2025, your water met state and federal drinking water requirements', yet the RTCR table marks Total Coliform compliance 'No' and discloses Level 1 and Level 2 assessments; both are recorded. Haloacetic acids and TTHM values are the highest quarterly locational running annual average; chlorine is the highest quarterly running annual average. The PFAS table's 'PHG (NL)' column prints California notification levels in parentheses, including '(1000)' for PFHxA and '(4.0)' for PFOA/PFOS, copied as printed. Magnesium and pH rows print no unit. Hardness appears twice (ppm and Grains/Gallon). PDF pages: lead/copper 3, primary 4, secondary and disinfection byproducts 5, additional parameters 6, PFAS 7, RTCR 8; page 14 'Where Your Water Comes From'."
}